# Everything here is read by FreeBSD: shell scripts, rc scripts, Python and
# configuration files. A CRLF checkout on Windows must not turn into a CRLF file
# on the firewall, where /bin/sh would read the carriage return as part of the
# command and an rc script would fail in a way nobody would guess from the error.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary

# What an appliance carries is the archive of a commit: the tarball the self-update downloads, and
# what xgs-image-builder puts into an image (its fetch-project.sh takes `git archive`). Nothing an
# appliance does not read goes into it: the documentation and its pictures, the workflows, the files
# about the project itself, and the repository's own tools, which run from a checkout here and in
# CI (2026-10-22). A file an appliance starts to read leaves this list in the same change.
docs/ export-ignore
.github/ export-ignore
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md export-ignore
CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
SECURITY.md export-ignore
DESIGN.md export-ignore
tools/ export-ignore
# README.md is left out too since 2026-10-30: nothing on an appliance reads it, and an image kept it
# beside the code (measured on an XGS 3300). LICENSE stays, the terms the code is given under.
/README.md export-ignore
